# [[fashionably|Fashionably]] [[distinguished#Adjective|distinguished]] or [[elegant]]; having an [[air#Noun|air]] of [[superiority]].
#* {{RQ:Reade Simpleton|volume=I|chapter=IX|page=57|passage=By the time the blue dress was tried on, Madame Cie had, with the aid of a few pins, plaits, and a bow of blue ribbon, transformed the half-lace shawl into one of the smartest and '''''distingué''''' things imaginable; but when the bill came in at Christmas, for that five minutes' labor and '''''distingué''''' touch, she charged one pound eight.}}
#* {{RQ:Stevenson Osbourne Wrecker|chapter=In which Jim and I Take Different Ways|page=179|passage=And she likes you so much, and thinks you so accomplished and '''distingué'''-looking, and was just as set as I was to have you for best man.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Emile Gaboriau|title=Mystery of Oricval|year=2001|page=158|passage=It was very noble, very '''distingue''', to ruin one's self without knowing how!}}

